---
title: "Theme Toggle"
description: "Lets people choose a light, dark or automatic color theme, and remembers the choice."
tags: [theme, accessibility, javascript]
usage: |
  `<theme-toggle>` is a custom element that wraps a form of radio buttons, one per
  theme. Register it once, then use it in your markup:

  ```js
  import { ThemeToggle } from "./theme-toggle.js";

  customElements.define(ThemeToggle.tagName, ThemeToggle);
  ```

  Attributes:

  - `target`: selector of the element that gets `data-theme`, for example
    `:root`.
  - `store="localStorage"`: remember the choice across visits.
  - `autodetect`: read the available themes from the radio buttons.
  - `enable`: enable the form controls once the element has loaded. Render them
    `disabled` so they do nothing without JavaScript.

  While it starts the element has a `loading` attribute, then `loaded`.
accessibility: |
  - The choices are native radio buttons in a `<fieldset>` with a `<legend>`, so
    they are grouped and announced together.
  - The controls stay disabled until the script runs, so they never appear to
    work when they cannot.
---

<theme-toggle target=":root" store="localStorage" autodetect enable>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">
  <form action="/theme/update" method="post">
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Theme</legend>
      <menu id="theme-menu">
        <li>
          <input
            id="theme-auto"
            type="radio"
            name="theme"
            value="auto"
            checked
            disabled
          > <label
            for="theme-auto"
          >Auto (system)</label>
        </li>
        <li>
          <input
            id="theme-light"
            type="radio"
            name="theme"
            value="light"
            disabled
          >
          <label for="theme-light">Light</label>
        </li>
        <li>
          <input
            id="theme-dark"
            type="radio"
            name="theme"
            value="dark"
            disabled
          >
          <label for="theme-dark">Dark</label>
        </li>
      </menu>
      <button disabled>Save Theme</button>
    </fieldset>
  </form>
</theme-toggle>

<script type="module">
  import { ThemeToggle } from "./theme-toggle.js";

  if (!customElements.get(ThemeToggle.tagName)) {
    customElements.define(ThemeToggle.tagName, ThemeToggle);
  }
</script>
